From 3aa59c03834d489b251908b8d831872f7e13cf73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Kuraev <naoru.desu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 75/75] temp/usb-signaller: fork to keep the USB host role at
 boot

usb-signaller 0.4.3 switches the USB role from host to device when it applies its default mode at startup and when it stops. When a USB-C hub or monitor is attached at boot, the Type-C port controller often picks host role before usb-signaller starts, so the hub and everything behind it, such as a monitor's touchscreen, stay off until plugged in again. Fork it with a patch that defers the default mode while the role is host and applies it once a USB device controller appears, and that leaves the role alone on stop.
